{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin","id":1547696,"title":"The Ahi-i-Batin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-12T11:54:27-08:00","id":1547696,"title":"The Ahi-i-Batin","content":"They are probably the best tradition with the best back-story(Book of Shadows) and underrated in M:tA. Yeah, they were used in Dark Ages: Mage, sans the Euthanatos backstory. Of course, the Order of Hermes has the most material, just because that's their flagship Order, I remember from Ars Magica. <br /> <br /> What's your favorite tradition out of MtA? <br /> <br /> As for DA: Mage, for me, well, I kinda like them all. They have a lot of use in a Dark Ages Game, but, I like the Ascension-system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T15:31:29-08:00","id":1547706,"title":"","content":"I like all the Traditions too. I really don\u2019t have a favorite. Depends on my mood which one I want to play, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T18:17:48-08:00","id":1547708,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely attracted to the Hermetics and the Etherites. I suppose it goes back to my childhood. I was awfully fond of Grandpa Munster and wanted him to teach me mad science and sorcery. The first fantasy novel I read was &quot;A Wizard of Earthsea,&quot; followed by &quot;The Sword in the Stone.&quot; I loved Golden Age Sci Fi. When I saw Catweezal on PBS with a Wizard talking about &quot;electrickery&quot; I was permanently hooked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T13:15:56-08:00","id":1547718,"title":"","content":"Etherites and Hermetics are my favorites for how they approach magic, how they enact it, and their attitudes. The &quot;slightly unmoored scientist whose mind moves faster than his good sense&quot; and the &quot;wise man/smart ass who would be arrogant except its not arrogant when its true*&quot; are some of my favorite characters to play.<br /> <br /> *Thinking of it, I've played an abnormal number of dragons in my years RPing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T15:35:52-08:00","id":1547720,"title":"","content":"Probably order of hermes and the valderman. Im a big fan of wizard classic and they cover a lot of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T19:56:28-08:00","id":1547724,"title":"","content":"While I'm personally very fond of the Virtual Adepts and Euthanatos (<b>post-First Edition version</b>,) my favorite characters played by others in games I run are a Son of Ether and Hermetic. The former, one Dr. Gregory McVitty, is the sole surviving/non-retired character who's featured since the beginning of our longest running chronicle for over seventeen years. He's also the only character in any of them who's had the Archmaster chair pulled out for him by his Tradition's emeriti, mainly because after all the man has accomplished it became unrealistic at a certain point for them not to make that offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T10:22:09-08:00","id":1547742,"title":"","content":"Me, I've developed a distaste for Traditions in general. I'm not fond of politics, and as of M20 that's what the Traditions are mainly good for. In particular, they're no longer needed as a stand-in for Paradigm and Practice. <br /> <br /> The type of mage that's my favorite, though, is the one outlined in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/367375/paradigm-explored-number-and-shape\" target=\"_blank\">Paradigm Explored: Number and Shape</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T15:58:05-08:00","id":1547766,"title":"","content":"I don't like Mage/Mage politics, as they are on each other's side, in a quest for Ascension; I view mages as philosophers, that may argue, but have no real goals other than knowledge: however, there are deranged mages out there. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin?p=1547724#post1547724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm personally very fond of the Virtual Adepts and Euthanatos (<b>post-First Edition version</b>,) . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that; 1st edition Euthanatos seem the same as 2nd. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T13:47:34-08:00","id":1547780,"title":"","content":"Philosophy is intensly political<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T15:28:36-08:00","id":1547783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin?p=1547780#post1547780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophy is intensly political</div> </div> </div> </div>Most things, taken seriously, are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T16:28:14-08:00","id":1547786,"title":"","content":"I'm also reading about the Taft\u00e2ni, which I didn't even know existed until last night. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin?p=1547780#post1547780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophy is intensly political</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, only about 25% of it is, if you take into account historical-philosophy. Most of philosophy is, &quot;Pepper is sold here and in Rome&quot;: (Is it the same pepper or the concept of, &quot;Pepper&quot;).<br /> <br /> And I'll never forget my Poli-Sci professor's definition of Politics: <i>&quot;Who gets what, when, where and how&quot;.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 01-16-2025, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-18T13:22:50-08:00","id":1547816,"title":"","content":"Easily my favorite Tradition is the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> Setting aside I like the idea of the traditional fantasy trope of the Wizard wearing a pointed hat, I made brief forays into Real Life Hermetic practices back when I first got into Mage. (Coming at MtAs through Vampire, by way of the Tremere, helped bias me toward this). I didn't get very far into these studies, but I found the systems of the Golden Dawn fascinating. And what we call &quot;Hermetic&quot; magic is a massive goulash of dozens of independent magical traditions (Alchemy, Kabbala, Tarot, Astrology, Enochian, etc.), giving Hermetic Mages a wide arsenal to draw from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T04:32:27-08:00","id":1547844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin?p=1547766#post1547766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like Mage/Mage politics, as they are on each other's side, in a quest for Ascension; I view mages as philosophers, that may argue, but have no real goals other than knowledge: however, there are deranged mages out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why is that; 1st edition Euthanatos seem the same as 2nd.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's been quite a long time since I've even looked at the first edition Mage core book, but I distinctly recall the Euthanatos being the least fleshed out Tradition concept in its initial presentation. My almost immediate impression was that, the way they were initially described, their inclusion was little more than an attempt to be &quot;edgy&quot; (the word people most often seem to use for it now,) and it wasn't until later writings that they were really made more &quot;three dimensional&quot; and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-26T18:20:20-08:00","id":1547966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547696-the-ahi-i-batin?p=1547844#post1547844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been quite a long time since I've even looked at the first edition Mage core book, but I distinctly recall the Euthanatos being the least fleshed out Tradition concept in its initial presentation. My almost immediate impression was that, the way they were initially described, their inclusion was little more than an attempt to be &quot;edgy&quot; (the word people most often seem to use for it now,) and it wasn't until later writings that they were really made more &quot;three dimensional&quot; and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that; when I first read about them, I just assumed, entropy-guys, etc. etc. They fleshed them out a bit more by the Book of Shadows, but excluded them by Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T03:15:38-08:00","id":1547996,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Dark Ages excluded a number of (proto-)Traditions. There's nothing equivalent to the Akashic Brotherhood there, nor any Cult of Ecstasy or Solificati. <br /> <br /> With that said, V20 gave us a Euthanatoic Fellowship in their Black Hand supplement. While it's not a Mage book, it's consistent enough with what DAMage did that I wouldn't have a problem including them in a DAMage chronicle, providing a storyline that somehow involved India.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}